      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_City%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1834 New Garden became Newport, renamed Fountain City in 1878 for its natural springs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_City%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Levi Coffin House, home of Quaker abolitionist Levi Coffin, was a key Underground Railroad stop.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_City%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Fountain City officially incorporated as a town in 1844, solidifying its early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
